Z||000000||GT Bastard||07-09-2000||04:35 PM||||Anybody know who's got the best price for the rockers designed for the V6?  (not the smallblock ones...) thanks!||||reg||12
Z||000001||Shaun41178||07-09-2000||04:40 PM||||You are talking about the Ture Roller rockers sold by Crane right?  I have seen them sold from Summit for $365.  Jegs is probably the same price.<P>Carparts.com can get them I am sure.  1/3 off and you would be saving $100 with the code for carparts.<P>I was going to use them on my 3.2 build up but I couldn't justify the extra expense of them for the power that they might give.  I would only expect 5 or so extra hp from the reduced friction in the higher rpms like 6k or so.  They would be nice to have though and if i could get them cheap I would use them but $365 is just too much for me<P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||07-09-2000||06:23 PM||||Why not use the ones for the small block? I've seen them on ebay for as little as 100 bucks, including locks and some even come with studs. You can drill and tap the holes to accept the 7/16" studs, and the offset is only about .030 from what I understand, plenty close for rollers.....||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||07-09-2000||07:11 PM||||Jegs has the best price at $306. Be prepared to wait for a long time for them. I ordered mine From PAW three months ago and they are finally being shipped the 14th. PAW's price is $320, I didn't know about Jegs at the time I ordered them.||||reg||1
